qsh for Debian
==============

This directory is upstream's Debian packaging; it lives in the upstream repository as
packaging/debian/ and is copied to debian/ to build:

    cp -r packaging/debian debian
    dpkg-buildpackage -us -uc                       # dependencies from librust-*-dev
    dpkg-buildpackage -us -uc -P pkg.qsh.vendored   # dependencies from vendor/

Binary packages: qsh-client (qsh) and qsh-server (qsh-server and its systemd user unit), split
like openssh-client / openssh-server and mosh, so servers need not carry the client.

Generated files: man/*.1, man/*.5 and completions/* are generated from the command-line
definitions upstream (`cargo xtask gen`, checked in upstream CI) and committed to the repository;
the release tarball contains them. The generator (the xtask crate) is not built here.

Dependencies, default build: every crate qsh uses (tokio, quinn, rustls with ring, rcgen, clap,
serde, serde_json, libc, zeroize, toml) through the archive's librust-*-dev packages and dh-cargo. The
workspace also contains xtask, whose dependencies (clap_mangen, clap_complete) cargo has to
resolve even though it is not built, hence their Build-Depends.

Dependencies, pkg.qsh.vendored: the crates come from a second orig tarball,
qsh_VERSION.orig-vendor.tar.xz (`cargo vendor --locked --versioned-dirs`, top directory vendor/),
and plain cargo builds against it offline. debian/copyright has one Files: vendor/NAME-VERSION/*
paragraph per crate, generated from Cargo.lock by packaging/ci/debian-copyright.py upstream.
dh_clean is told to keep vendor/*/Cargo.toml.orig, which cargo checks against the vendored
checksums. Upstream CI builds this way on Debian 12 and 13 and Ubuntu 24.04
(packaging/ci/debian.sh).

Rust: rust-version is 1.85 (Debian 13's rustc). On older releases (backports) the vendored
build works with a newer toolchain on PATH and `dpkg-buildpackage -d`, or with Ubuntu's
versioned rustc-1.NN packages.

The cargo feature self-install (`qsh install HOST`, which downloads release binaries) is not
enabled: the Debian build performs no network access at build time or at runtime.

